# Lab shell

Skill labs live under `/lab/<name>`. Hybrid Connection is `/lab/hybrid`. `/hybrid` only redirects there.

The stage bar (`components/stage-nav.tsx`, `components/stage-shell.tsx`) is two rows and there is no footer. The first row is Living Morphologies and the Edit control. The second row is the workspaces on the left and that workspace’s tabs on the right. The workspaces keep the bordered treatment. The tabs are smaller, with no box, so they do not compete with the workspaces. A lab screen does not add another page title, a header bar, a footer, or site navigation. A title sits inside its frame. Tools that belong to the work sit in the work. The Living Morphologies title returns to the website. The stage bar does not repeat Home, Overall Workflow, or Results. Desktop mode is archived. Presentation is the only live lab scale, and the website stays on its Classroom pair. Edit stays on that row so the presentation canvas can be zoomed and panned. The desktop/presentation switch remains in the code. Set `DESKTOP_MODE_ARCHIVED` to false in `components/display-sync.ts` to restore it.

Empty black space is a designed element, not leftover space. Plan it in every layout, on the website and in the labs. Leave it inside bigger frames, between the tiles, plates, and iterations they hold, and between the bigger frames themselves. Space between groups is larger than space within a group, so the categories read first. Never pack frames edge to edge. When content must fit, make the items smaller before you remove the space.

Filament is the ink control inside each archetype. It is not a stage on the stage bar, and it stays off the presentation front end.

If a skill needs a different address, a second header or footer, or any other departure from this shell:

1. Stop the edit.
2. Tell the user the departure, and why this rule exists: one shell keeps the labs cohesive, so later skills match the same header, footer, and presentation frame.
3. Wait for the user to approve the departure or keep the shell.

When the shell itself is refined, update this rule so the next skill follows the current base.
